  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to MOT (If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> is internuclear axis) The configuration of<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>CN</mtext><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>*</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>*</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math><br />&nbsp;<br />Bond order<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electrons</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bonding</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>orbitals</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electrons</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>anti</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>bonding</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>orbitals</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math> <mrow> <mtext>Bond&#160;order&#160;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>CN</mtext></mrow> <mo>&#8722;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> is diamagnetic due to absence of unpaired electron.</p>"
